# Pairs with ListedInSink. The pass reserves a doomed id only when it
# removes the id's row, not when it decides the doom. Between the two, a
# republish of the id is admitted, rewrites its manifest and registers it
# again after the pass has removed the row; the pass then deletes the sink
# manifest of a backup the catalog lists.
MODULE: ListedInSinkReserveAfterRowRemoval
TARGET: ListedInSink
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the pass reserves a doomed id only at its row removal
PERTURBS: Acquire

--- FIND
    /\ \A p \in Passes : cap[c].id \notin prDoomed[p]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: the reservation starts at the row removal.
    /\ \A p \in Passes : cap[c].id \notin prGone[p]
--- END
